# More than one document at once (ADR-0396), which is what makes this editor
# usable on the compiler it was written for: `pascalc` translates every 6.13
# program-component, and this compiler is three of them, so a diagnostic
# naming a file that is not on screen is the ordinary case.
#
# The claims, in the order the keys drive them:
#
#   - F3 asks for a name, in the same framed box `Find` and `Save as` use --
#     a fourth user of ADR-0391's primitives and no new machinery;
#   - answering it makes a *second* document current, and the status line
#     starts saying which of how many, having said nothing while there was
#     only one;
#   - F6 goes to the next and wraps, and each document keeps its own cursor,
#     its own scroll and its own dirty mark, because switching is one
#     whole-record assignment each way and cannot drop a field;
#   - an undo does **not** reach across a switch: the journal is per document,
#     so Ctrl-Z here reverses the edit made here and not the one made there;
#   - and a diagnostic naming an *open* document is landed on -- the cursor
#     goes to the other file and the status line follows it.
#
# The session drives no files: `push` fills a buffer the way loading one
# does, and `open` is what the shell would have been asked to do. That is
# ADR-0381's line -- the model decides which document, the shell reads bytes.
name a.pas
size 10 30
push program a(output);
push begin
push   writeln(1)
push end.
draw
func 3
draw
keys b.pas
ctrl M
draw
push program b(output);
push begin
push end.
esc B
esc B
keys X
draw
func 6
draw
ctrl Z
draw
fault b.pas:2:3: error: something in the other file
draw
